# The STM32 firmware toolchain.
#
# docs/design/seam.md: the BYTES are baked
# into the image unconditionally; the interactive provision phase asks whether
# to ENABLE the dev role (the reflex-fw checkout, PATH exposure, the udev rules
# being active) -- not whether to install it.
#
# Installing these at provision time instead would put a package mirror back on
# the recovery path, which is the one thing docs/design/seam.md exists to remove.
# Disk is cheap; a network in a machine shop on the day the SD card died is not.
#
# So STAGE_LIST is NOT the mechanism here. This stage always runs.

